  "rationale": "The batch repeatedly reveals nouns after adjectives, including adjective phrases after possessives and determiners (for example, “Lily’s red scissors,” “the small needles,” and “the red pears”). The current noun roots give little support to this general context when no preceding-verb feature is available, leaving the target noun poorly ranked. Add a modest shared-context rule to noun outputs rather than favoring one observed noun or name. This should help the noun class while retaining lexical alternatives. Counterexamples include adjective uses that are nominalized or followed by something other than a noun; the modest weight preserves those alternatives. The preceding weight-only update improved batch loss only slightly, so this is a compact structural hypothesis, not a claim that it passed replay.",
